  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacities of national constituents to stimulate enterprise development for job creation including improving working conditions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Productivity gaps, widespread informality, and limited access to inclusive business support services remain major challenges for micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs) and workers in Ethiopia. These constraints affect both agricultural and non-agricultural sectors and are compounded by low productivity, weak compliance with labour and environmental standards, gender inequalities, and limited access to finance, markets, and quality services.

During the biennium, the CPO supports improved productivity and working conditions through action plans in selected sectors, while promoting responsible business conduct and the application of international labour standards. It advances climate-responsive practices, occupational safety and health, and measures to prevent child and forced labour. The programme also facilitates national and international dialogue, including in line with the ILO MNE Declaration, to strengthen due diligence and responsible business practices in priority value chains.

The CPO further contributes to inclusive enterprise development by strengthening the capacity of public institutions and business development service providers, including the Kaizen Excellence Center, to deliver productivity-enhancing, ESG-aligned, and inclusive services to MSMEs. It supports selected value chains and expands access to entrepreneurship and financial services for entrepreneurs, cooperatives, and small enterprises, including refugees and host communities.

The programme benefits MSMEs, cooperatives, workers, and aspiring entrepreneurs, with particular attention to women, youth, and vulnerable groups. It also strengthens the capacity of institutions and social partners to improve labour market governance, promote social dialogue, and support inclusive and sustainable enterprise development.

Aligned with Ethiopia&#x2019;s Ten-Year Development Plan (2021&#x2013;2030), the CPO contributes to productive employment, enterprise formalization, and inclusive economic growth.</narrative>
  </description>
